      ":question/id": "b8f1a0a3-0b71-52cd-b327-6c0ec92e34be",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105672",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vector field $F={e}^{y+z}\\,i+j+xyz\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,1,-1).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{y+z} & 1 & xyz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y+z})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y+z})]k \\\\  & =(xz-0)i-(yz-{e}^{y+z})j+(0-{e}^{y+z})k \\\\  & =xz\\,i+({e}^{y+z}-yz)j-{e}^{y+z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,1,-1) & =2(-1)\\,i+({e}^{1+(-1)}-1(-1))j-{e}^{1+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
