      ":question/id": "2c3cbbe9-4c45-5e2a-804f-38b6dd4503b8",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131336",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}\\,i+yz\\,j+{e}^{yz}\\,k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x{e}^{yz} & yz & {e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{yz})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{yz})]k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i-(0-xy{e}^{yz})\\,j+(0-xz{e}^{yz})\\,k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
